## TEMPLATE — copy this file to `net_secrets.gd` (same folder, drop the
## `.example`) and paste your own key in. That copy is gitignored.
##
## Firebase Web API keys are not secrets in the usual sense: the key identifies
## the project rather than authorising anything, it ships inside every client
## build, and access is decided by the security rules in
## firebase/database.rules.json plus Auth. It lives outside version control
## anyway, for two practical reasons:
##   - secret scanners match the AIza... pattern regardless, and alerts that get
##     routinely dismissed train you to dismiss the real ones too
##   - it keeps a per-developer / per-environment key a one-file change
##
## Because it is NOT a resource Godot generates, remember: this file must exist
## locally for the project to run, and it IS included in exported builds.
##
## Recommended alongside this (Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services ->
## Credentials -> your key -> API restrictions): restrict the key to
## "Identity Toolkit API" and "Token Service API" only. Do NOT add an Android
## application restriction — it would reject the desktop client and break
## testing from the editor.

extends RefCounted

const WEB_API_KEY := "PASTE-YOUR-FIREBASE-WEB-API-KEY-HERE"
